WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:04.267
Here are a few ways to
make Mindwtr fit your day.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:09.567
Capture a thought from a widget, Quick
Capture, or Siri and Shortcuts on Apple

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:10.333
devices.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.200
You can also bring in email, or record
a voice note and have it transcribed.

00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:16.267
It all lands in your Inbox.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:20.533
See your tasks alongside calendar
events when you plan the week.

00:00:20.833 --> 00:00:23.200
Use the board to move work between stages.

00:00:23.367 --> 00:00:26.100
Switch to the timeline for
a view across your projects.

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:28.800
You’re working with the
same tasks in each view.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:34.033
Use keyboard shortcuts to capture and
navigate without reaching for the mouse.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:37.267
Add Markdown notes when a task
needs a little more detail.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:44.400
Work offline, then choose how to sync:
Dropbox, iCloud, a folder, WebDAV, or your

00:00:44.433 --> 00:00:45.133
own server.

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:49.800
End-to-end encryption is optional
for Dropbox, WebDAV, and file sync.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:56.333
AI, MCP, Pomodoro and automation
are optional and off by default.

00:00:56.633 --> 00:00:58.733
Turn on only what’s useful to you.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:05.900
You’ll also find themes, languages, Obsidian
integration, import and export, sharing, a

00:01:05.967 --> 00:01:07.667
web app—and more.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.967
Explore Mindwtr at mindwtr.app.
